From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:30:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] AML MVC: start at a picture with its own SPS and PPS

A resume or a seek in Pacific Rim (3D Blu-ray remux, mk3d) that landed at
12:11.773 never showed a picture: the MVC decoder took the IDR and the
pictures after it but output none, and the player waited on it for good.
The same film resumed half a second earlier played.

The file's header (avcC + mvcC) carries a PPS for each view that differs
from the ones in the stream (28ea805fcc03 / 284aadf300c0 against
28ea83f300c0 / 284aad3f300c). About 60% of the IDRs repeat the stream's
SPS and PPS, at most 0.84 s apart; the rest carry none and rely on the
ones before. Played through, the decoder has the stream's. Opened or
flushed at an IDR without them, it has only the header's, which the
bitstream converter puts in front of that IDR, and with those the MVC
decoder outputs nothing.

So after an open, MVC pictures are dropped until one carries its own SPS,
subset SPS and PPS (both views'), for two seconds of pictures at most; a
file that never repeats them then starts from the header as before. A
flush (seek, chapter) waits again only once the stream's own sets have
turned out to differ from the header's (a set not found verbatim in the
header): a file whose sets are the header's, or that has none, loses no
pictures on a seek. Only MVC: H.264 and HEVC decode whatever IDR they
start at.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
